Google Cloud Storage V4 conformance fixtures

Source: https://github.com/googleapis/conformance-tests, commit
bd81c3038308486dc1004e268fdab4391829ee78, storage/v1/v4_signatures.json
(SHA-256 5da2708039e2cf17173a031838e3448509d801ba4ce1577fde79970c072178fe)
and storage/v1/test_service_account.not-a-test.json. The repository is
licensed under Apache-2.0; a copy is in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

v4_signatures.json retains the first 17 signingV4Tests unchanged and omits
all postPolicyV4Tests. Every retained expected canonical request, string to
sign and complete URL is checked byte for byte. The accompanying test key
is Google's explicitly inactive, public dummy key; only its type, client
email and private key fields are retained. Tests provide their own local
HTTPS token URI, and never send a request using the fixture's URL.

Not included from the upstream signing file:
Virtual Hosted Style; HTTP Bucket Bound Hostname Support; HTTPS Bucket Bound
Hostname Support; Simple GET with hostname; Simple GET with non-default
hostname; Simple GET with endpoint on client; Endpoint on client with scheme;
Emulator host; Endpoint on client takes precedence over emulator; Hostname
takes precendence over endpoint and emulator; Universe domain; Universe
domain with virtual hosted style. The library offers path-style endpoint
overrides; these specific hostname, precedence and virtual-host variants are
not covered by the vendored vectors.

Post-policy signing is outside this library's surface. Omitted upstream
scenarios: POST Policy Simple; POST Policy Simple Virtual Hosted Style; POST
Policy Simple Bucket Bound Hostname; POST Policy Simple Bucket Bound Hostname
HTTP; POST Policy ACL matching; POST Policy Within Content-Range; POST Policy
Cache-Control File Header; POST Policy Success With Status; POST Policy
Success With Redirect; POST Policy Character Escaping; POST Policy With
Additional Metadata.
